[SPEAKER_02]: Not specifically through the eye, but you could say through the mental eye.

205
00:13:01,553 --> 00:13:02,894
[SPEAKER_02]: There has to be an image there.

206
00:13:03,334 --> 00:13:13,077
[SPEAKER_02]: Even if you were, like, blind your whole life, you will have to have an image of your experience as a whole of consuming some object in your mouth that was producing the salty taste for you.

207
00:13:14,437 --> 00:13:19,619
[SPEAKER_02]: But you can't imagine the pure saltiness in itself.

208
00:13:20,922 --> 00:13:22,183
[SPEAKER_02]: But that's beside the point now.

209
00:13:22,403 --> 00:13:24,604
[SPEAKER_02]: Are these particular senses which come first?

210
00:13:24,664 --> 00:13:25,205
[SPEAKER_02]: Doesn't matter.

211
00:13:25,545 --> 00:13:27,566
[SPEAKER_02]: Whichever way they come, an image has to be there.

212
00:13:28,086 --> 00:13:33,350
[SPEAKER_02]: And if people were confused, why would you be describing the perception in terms of colors, these images?

213
00:13:33,390 --> 00:13:35,191
[SPEAKER_02]: It's because, yeah, that's what it would boil down to.

214
00:13:36,602 --> 00:13:38,543
[SPEAKER_02]: And you can describe it also in terms of space.

215
00:13:38,623 --> 00:13:41,224
[SPEAKER_02]: That's where space is sometimes listed as one of the elements.

216
00:13:42,024 --> 00:13:49,747
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not fundamentally an element, like four Mahābhūtas, but it's out there with consciousness and other Mahābhūtas.

217
00:13:49,807 --> 00:13:53,068
[SPEAKER_02]: So, like the six elements.

218
00:13:58,169 --> 00:14:05,572
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you said, why everything, every image has a color?

219
00:14:07,607 --> 00:14:09,488
[SPEAKER_02]: If you... First, every image is.

220
00:14:11,108 --> 00:14:15,449
[SPEAKER_02]: Because now, when you think every image has a color, they are saying color, it's another image for you.

221
00:14:16,029 --> 00:14:20,010
[SPEAKER_02]: So, what you're really saying is, every image has an image.

222
00:14:20,070 --> 00:14:22,371
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's true, but that's not practically accurate.

223
00:14:23,711 --> 00:14:30,073
[SPEAKER_02]: So, there is an image within which you discern the properties of color, characteristics of its being manifested.

224
00:14:36,471 --> 00:14:38,892
[SPEAKER_02]: So, think space.

225
00:14:38,912 --> 00:14:42,154
[SPEAKER_02]: When I say space, what image is present in your mind?

226
00:14:46,035 --> 00:14:46,335
[SPEAKER_02]: Space.

227
00:14:46,896 --> 00:14:47,216
[SPEAKER_02]: Space.

228
00:14:47,876 --> 00:14:49,457
[SPEAKER_02]: What's present in your mind?

229
00:14:49,477 --> 00:14:51,118
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, something clear.

230
00:14:51,898 --> 00:14:52,398
[SPEAKER_02]: Something clear.

231
00:14:52,778 --> 00:14:55,219
[SPEAKER_02]: When I say space, what's present in my mind is the word space.

232
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:56,380
[SPEAKER_02]: Literally.

233
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:59,021
[SPEAKER_02]: Written word space is what's present in my mind.

234
00:14:59,361 --> 00:15:00,862
[SPEAKER_02]: But, yeah, whatever...

235
00:15:00,902 --> 00:15:02,743
[SPEAKER_02]: I was thinking expansive, sort of...

236
00:15:04,632 --> 00:15:06,133
[SPEAKER_02]: The point is, there has to be an image.

237
00:15:06,494 --> 00:15:07,915
[SPEAKER_02]: There has to be an image.

238
00:15:08,055 --> 00:15:24,208
[SPEAKER_02]: If I say, I don't know, a term in another language that you don't understand, you still have to have an image in your mind of, based on the basis of sound that I just produced at you, you will have an image of

239
00:15:26,032 --> 00:15:27,713
[SPEAKER_02]: What does that mean?

240
00:15:28,073 --> 00:15:31,075
[SPEAKER_02]: Is this gibberish or this particular language?

241
00:15:31,275 --> 00:15:33,777
[SPEAKER_02]: You have to have some image, always.

242
00:15:33,797 --> 00:15:39,800
[SPEAKER_02]: There is no such thing as an imageless mind, unless neither perception nor perception and so on.

243
00:15:39,981 --> 00:15:43,723
[SPEAKER_02]: Even space, basis of infinite space is basis of infinite image.

244
00:15:44,283 --> 00:15:44,483
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

245
00:15:44,783 --> 00:15:46,324
[SPEAKER_02]: Image of infiniteness of space.

246
00:15:46,924 --> 00:15:52,046
[SPEAKER_01]: But ordinarily, even if you're not there, there's something's going on.

247
00:15:52,066 --> 00:15:52,667
[SPEAKER_01]: There's an image.

248
00:15:52,827 --> 00:15:56,028
[SPEAKER_01]: Within that image, you will discern various perceptions.

249
00:15:56,128 --> 00:15:58,349
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, within that image, you'll discern the five senses.

250
00:15:58,729 --> 00:15:59,109
[SPEAKER_02]: That's what I mean.

251
00:15:59,129 --> 00:16:01,870
[SPEAKER_02]: Within that image, you'll discern more images.

252
00:16:01,890 --> 00:16:02,091
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

253
00:16:02,511 --> 00:16:04,652
[SPEAKER_02]: Within that image, you'll discern your intentions.

254
00:16:04,852 --> 00:16:05,052
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

255
00:16:05,392 --> 00:16:05,572
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

256
00:16:07,990 --> 00:16:14,552
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's a kind of a sort of starting image, which is basically the image of this experience.

257
00:16:14,652 --> 00:16:18,074
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, and the starting image does not disappear when the second thing comes in.

258
00:16:18,094 --> 00:16:18,254
[SPEAKER_02]: No, no.

259
00:16:18,274 --> 00:16:25,296
[SPEAKER_02]: The starting image remains as a primary soul, only container, in which, yeah, you can't be outside of it.

260
00:16:25,656 --> 00:16:27,857
[SPEAKER_02]: That's where the mind comes first, the image comes first.

261
00:16:28,915 --> 00:16:35,462
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the primary image... You thinking outside of... there's outside of this image, then, in yours, is another image, within this image.

262
00:16:35,482 --> 00:16:38,124
[SPEAKER_00]: The image that you have is the experience as a whole.

263
00:16:38,344 --> 00:16:38,625
[SPEAKER_00]: Sorry?

264
00:16:38,785 --> 00:16:39,986
[SPEAKER_00]: The experience as a whole.

265
00:16:40,386 --> 00:16:43,510
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, of course, that's what the image... like, experience as a whole.

266
00:16:43,590 --> 00:16:45,792
[SPEAKER_02]: When I say, imagine your experience as a whole.

267
00:16:48,044 --> 00:16:55,448
[SPEAKER_02]: Or, don't imagine your experience as a whole, come back to the body, be here now, present, be present moment.

268
00:16:55,608 --> 00:16:58,350
[SPEAKER_02]: What is present with you in the most acute sense?

269
00:16:59,170 --> 00:17:09,516
[SPEAKER_02]: You are not specifically looking, looking, well, I might be doing, if I'm doing some sort of meditation technique, but if I'm not falling into that trap, and so you just want to be present,

270
00:17:11,063 --> 00:17:13,304
[SPEAKER_02]: What is the closest thing to you?

271
00:17:13,984 --> 00:17:18,125
[SPEAKER_00]: It's an image of this experience as a whole.

272
00:17:18,745 --> 00:17:19,865
[SPEAKER_02]: So that's the point.

273
00:17:20,225 --> 00:17:23,466
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't really have anything other than that, even if you want to.

274
00:17:23,986 --> 00:17:28,727
[SPEAKER_02]: But the problem is when you have images, yet here you are, thinking you're observing the actual form.

275
00:17:29,308 --> 00:17:31,728
[SPEAKER_02]: You think you're observing the matter, the reality behind.

276
00:17:31,748 --> 00:17:34,709
[SPEAKER_02]: You think you're observing physical sensations and whatnot.

277
00:17:35,509 --> 00:17:49,514
[SPEAKER_02]: All you're observing is images enduring, on account of which you end up misconceiving those images as matter, misconceiving those images as feelings, as perceptions, as intentions, as... basically, misconceiving the aggregates.

278
00:17:50,774 --> 00:17:55,075
[SPEAKER_02]: Or rather, conceiving the aggregates, giving them the being, assuming them, appropriating them.

279
00:17:58,836 --> 00:18:00,457
[SPEAKER_02]: Think about me, myself.

280
00:18:03,328 --> 00:18:06,410
[SPEAKER_02]: Can you even think that without an image?

281
00:18:06,510 --> 00:18:12,435
[SPEAKER_02]: A certain degree, a certain independence of, like, aspect of that thought, I am.

282
00:18:13,015 --> 00:18:18,299
[SPEAKER_02]: There's a certain shape to it, that usually gets associated with your own face.

283
00:18:20,201 --> 00:18:22,442
[SPEAKER_02]: It's like a veil in the background.

284
00:18:22,462 --> 00:18:23,823
[SPEAKER_02]: But the point is, an image is there.

285
00:18:23,843 --> 00:18:27,706
[SPEAKER_02]: It doesn't matter how ambiguous, how subtle, image has to be there.

286
00:18:28,567 --> 00:18:32,370
[SPEAKER_02]: And not being trained in regard to those images means not being trained in regard to your mind.

287
00:18:34,125 --> 00:18:40,209
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's how you will always then be governed by the kind of these assumed directions that these images take you.

288
00:18:41,289 --> 00:18:46,972
[SPEAKER_02]: Image of my face means me, I am, my control, master, owner, appropriator.

289
00:18:47,593 --> 00:18:48,333
[SPEAKER_01]: All that's implied.

290
00:18:48,774 --> 00:18:50,715
[SPEAKER_02]: Not seeing it, you took it upon yourself.

291
00:18:55,297 --> 00:18:56,438
[SPEAKER_02]: So, leave your mind blank.

292
00:18:58,839 --> 00:18:59,280
[SPEAKER_02]: What is that?

293
00:19:01,829 --> 00:19:02,169
[SPEAKER_02]: You can.

294
00:19:02,629 --> 00:19:03,049
[SPEAKER_01]: What is that?

295
00:19:03,249 --> 00:19:04,750
[SPEAKER_02]: It's another image.

296
00:19:05,870 --> 00:19:07,070
[SPEAKER_02]: So, yeah, it's not truly blank.

297
00:19:08,210 --> 00:19:17,832
[SPEAKER_02]: Because, well, but how can you even designate blankness, unless it's absence of something else, which is then an image present in your mind in regard to this, which is absence of that image.

298
00:19:20,573 --> 00:19:21,993
[SPEAKER_02]: Think about the empty room.

299
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:30,955
[SPEAKER_02]: So, see, that's the whole, the sign of emptiness that the Buddha was talking about.

300
00:19:32,630 --> 00:19:40,215
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, imagine, like, when you go into the empty heart and you realize this place is empty of other people.

301
00:19:41,535 --> 00:19:47,359
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's actually factually perceiving an image of absence of others.

302
00:19:47,599 --> 00:19:50,121
[SPEAKER_02]: Fully develop that image and then apply it to yourself.

303
00:19:50,821 --> 00:19:58,766
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, so, so is this experience as a whole, in its entirety, this image is absent of persons.

304
00:20:01,831 --> 00:20:09,173
[SPEAKER_02]: Because you clarified the sign of emptiness, the characteristics of emptiness, means you see there's a clear image.

305
00:20:10,133 --> 00:20:12,834
[SPEAKER_02]: Now you see it also pertaining to your own experience as a whole.

306
00:20:14,035 --> 00:20:18,016
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not empty, empty, just space out and drool, sort of, pass out unconscious.

307
00:20:18,716 --> 00:20:18,856
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

308
00:20:19,036 --> 00:20:19,896
[SPEAKER_02]: It's empty of this.

309
00:20:20,456 --> 00:20:22,377
[SPEAKER_02]: This experience is empty of lust.

310
00:20:22,637 --> 00:20:23,637
[SPEAKER_02]: It's empty of aversion.

311
00:20:23,717 --> 00:20:24,697
[SPEAKER_02]: It's empty of delusion.

312
00:20:28,258 --> 00:20:30,319
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if I say emptiness,

313
00:20:31,183 --> 00:20:32,144
[SPEAKER_02]: What's present in the mind?

314
00:20:34,526 --> 00:20:35,026
[SPEAKER_02]: Emptiness.

315
00:20:39,090 --> 00:20:42,192
[SPEAKER_02]: What image is there?

316
00:20:42,252 --> 00:20:42,773
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothingness.

317
00:20:43,733 --> 00:20:44,014
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay.

318
00:20:44,134 --> 00:20:46,456
[SPEAKER_02]: So, what are the characteristics of nothingness?

319
00:20:48,037 --> 00:20:48,998
Empty.

320
00:20:49,178 --> 00:20:49,818
[SPEAKER_02]: Empty space.

321
00:20:49,838 --> 00:20:51,480
[SPEAKER_02]: What is the characteristic of empty space?

322
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:52,901
[SPEAKER_02]: So, then the space is there.

323
00:20:53,341 --> 00:20:56,324
[SPEAKER_02]: So, there is a certain container, but it's empty.

324
00:20:57,845 --> 00:20:59,086
[SPEAKER_02]: So, things that...

325
00:20:59,126 --> 00:20:59,967
[SPEAKER_02]: Things could be in there.

326
00:21:01,379 --> 00:21:11,805
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, but the point is, so, things that are making the space empty, are there as absence, as a negative presence.

327
00:21:13,706 --> 00:21:17,608
[SPEAKER_02]: Because if there is nothing that could be in there, you wouldn't say this is empty of so.

328
00:21:18,229 --> 00:21:19,590
[SPEAKER_02]: It would just be this is so.

329
00:21:22,191 --> 00:21:23,892
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the nothingness of what then?

330
00:21:28,034 --> 00:21:28,675
[SPEAKER_00]: The nothingness...

331
00:21:30,795 --> 00:21:32,555
[SPEAKER_02]: When I ask you emptiness, what do you say?

332
00:21:32,615 --> 00:21:34,176
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, it's nothing, nothingness.

333
00:21:34,676 --> 00:21:36,536
[SPEAKER_02]: I say, well, what is the characteristic of nothingness?

334
00:21:37,277 --> 00:21:39,257
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay, characteristic is empty space.

335
00:21:40,177 --> 00:21:40,757
[SPEAKER_02]: Empty of what?

336
00:21:41,198 --> 00:21:41,738
[SPEAKER_02]: That space?

337
00:21:42,038 --> 00:21:42,598
[SPEAKER_02]: Empty of what?

338
00:21:42,718 --> 00:21:45,079
[SPEAKER_02]: What is the absence in that space, in that nothingness?

339
00:21:46,359 --> 00:21:51,180
[SPEAKER_02]: That comes to your mind when I keep repeating nothingness, nothingness, nothingness, nothingness.

340
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:56,421
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's not, there's not, there's absence of something.

341
00:21:57,782 --> 00:21:59,142
[SPEAKER_02]: Absence of something, well,

342
00:21:59,845 --> 00:22:01,205
[SPEAKER_02]: But that's already something, isn't it?

343
00:22:01,545 --> 00:22:02,026
[SPEAKER_02]: Nothingness.

344
00:22:02,626 --> 00:22:03,726
[SPEAKER_02]: What I said is something.

345
00:22:04,926 --> 00:22:09,287
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you can't say it's absence of something, because then it's not absence of itself.

346
00:22:09,307 --> 00:22:09,708
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

347
00:22:09,728 --> 00:22:18,250
[SPEAKER_02]: So, more specifically, nothingness, or emptiness, more accurately.

348
00:22:18,270 --> 00:22:18,870
[SPEAKER_02]: Empty of what?

349
00:22:22,851 --> 00:22:24,331
[SPEAKER_00]: Empty of everything else that's not there.

350
00:22:25,351 --> 00:22:27,092
[SPEAKER_02]: What are the characteristics of being empty?

351
00:22:28,218 --> 00:22:30,579
[SPEAKER_02]: Don't necessarily look for the... it's empty of this, this, this.

352
00:22:31,059 --> 00:22:37,802
[SPEAKER_02]: Characteristics of being empty, as we just described it, it has to be kind of negative.

353
00:22:38,182 --> 00:22:38,562
[SPEAKER_02]: Exactly.

354
00:22:39,262 --> 00:22:42,964
[SPEAKER_02]: Negative presence or presence of absence.

355
00:22:46,808 --> 00:22:48,869
[SPEAKER_00]: So, dwell on the presence of absence.

356
00:22:50,209 --> 00:22:51,449
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not really empty.

357
00:22:51,549 --> 00:22:56,571
[SPEAKER_02]: As in, it's not really empty and you assume external world of real absence of things, which is inconceivable.

358
00:22:57,311 --> 00:22:58,251
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not really empty.

359
00:22:59,052 --> 00:23:02,733
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't even finish that sentence if things were truly empty.

360
00:23:02,753 --> 00:23:03,633
[SPEAKER_02]: As in, don't exist.

361
00:23:05,114 --> 00:23:06,814
[SPEAKER_02]: Emptiness is not non-existence.

362
00:23:07,534 --> 00:23:09,335
[SPEAKER_02]: It's only emptiness of certain things.

363
00:23:10,458 --> 00:23:18,303
[SPEAKER_02]: People are used to, well, not seeing the images in their mind and then just just following the kind of the positive directions of craving, pretty much.

364
00:23:19,824 --> 00:23:21,625
[SPEAKER_02]: You say like it's a pure image.

365
00:23:22,606 --> 00:23:23,567
[SPEAKER_02]: Let's finish with this.

366
00:23:24,067 --> 00:23:26,328
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the point is emptiness.

367
00:23:27,249 --> 00:23:28,190
[SPEAKER_02]: It's an image in your mind.

368
00:23:28,590 --> 00:23:32,312
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, you can say, when I say emptiness, I just have a word emptiness written in my mind.

369
00:23:32,753 --> 00:23:36,335
[SPEAKER_02]: Big E. Okay, so what are the characteristics of something being empty?

370
00:23:36,355 --> 00:23:37,656
[SPEAKER_02]: You said, well, it's an empty space.

371
00:23:39,302 --> 00:23:39,562
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay.

372
00:23:39,662 --> 00:23:45,146
[SPEAKER_02]: Empty space is defined as an empty space by absence of that which is empty of.

373
00:23:46,287 --> 00:23:47,427
[SPEAKER_02]: That is its characteristic.

374
00:23:47,467 --> 00:23:49,169
[SPEAKER_02]: That's what definition of emptiness is.

375
00:23:49,289 --> 00:23:50,670
[SPEAKER_02]: Doesn't matter what is empty of.

376
00:23:52,651 --> 00:23:59,195
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's a negative presence or presence of the absence of certain things.

377
00:24:00,336 --> 00:24:01,297
[SPEAKER_02]: Dwell on that image.

378
00:24:02,276 --> 00:24:03,837
[SPEAKER_02]: Presence of absence, basically.

379
00:24:03,917 --> 00:24:07,478
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not a contradiction, because absence... ...is a thing.

380
00:24:07,518 --> 00:24:08,798
[SPEAKER_02]: ...is a thing, that is present.

381
00:24:09,339 --> 00:24:14,360
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's the content of that, that's not there, but the nature of absence is there.

382
00:24:16,801 --> 00:24:17,942
[SPEAKER_02]: What else does it mirror?

383
00:24:19,022 --> 00:24:24,144
[SPEAKER_02]: The same principle, in your experience, then.

384
00:24:24,244 --> 00:24:24,804
[SPEAKER_01]: Anatta.

385
00:24:25,445 --> 00:24:25,665
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

386
00:24:25,705 --> 00:24:26,545
[SPEAKER_02]: Sense of ownership.

387
00:24:32,027 --> 00:24:36,028
[SPEAKER_02]: sense of master, controller, because I am here.

388
00:24:36,508 --> 00:24:36,808
[SPEAKER_02]: Where?

389
00:24:37,669 --> 00:24:39,529
[SPEAKER_02]: What is the content of my sense of self?

390
00:24:40,029 --> 00:24:40,709
[SPEAKER_02]: Can you find it?

391
00:24:42,490 --> 00:24:44,891
[SPEAKER_02]: Can you find the content of what you are?

392
00:24:45,591 --> 00:24:46,351
[SPEAKER_02]: But you are.

393
00:24:46,371 --> 00:24:47,171
[SPEAKER_02]: It's always a negative.

394
00:24:47,491 --> 00:24:50,132
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the absence of content is your presence.

395
00:24:50,752 --> 00:24:53,733
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's why sense of self is assumed in regard to everything and nothing.

396
00:24:54,553 --> 00:25:00,675
[SPEAKER_02]: But once you started, oh, so the absence, sorry, the presence of the absence is a real image.

397
00:25:01,665 --> 00:25:06,126
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't need to keep chasing content and only to verify the image through finding the content.

398
00:25:06,146 --> 00:25:07,046
[SPEAKER_02]: No, it's the other way around.

399
00:25:08,847 --> 00:25:13,168
[SPEAKER_02]: So, by understanding the nature of emptiness, you get to understand the nature of anatta.

400
00:25:13,948 --> 00:25:20,750
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's why this room is empty of others, and his mind is established upon the perception of that image.

401
00:25:22,570 --> 00:25:23,931
[SPEAKER_02]: So is this body.

402
00:25:23,971 --> 00:25:28,852
[SPEAKER_02]: These five aggregates are empty of the self, as in the self master controller.

403
00:25:29,707 --> 00:25:30,067
[SPEAKER_02]: Empty.

404
00:25:30,528 --> 00:25:34,450
[SPEAKER_02]: So, there is the sense of self that is the present absence of the owner.

